    <h2>BOOKING CANCELLATION, RECEIPT SURRENDER &amp; FULL SETTLEMENT DEED</h2>
    <p class="subtitle">(To be executed on Non-Judicial Stamp Paper or appended with Stamp Paper)</p>

    <p>This Deed of Cancellation, Receipt Surrender and Full Settlement is executed on this <strong>______ day of __________________, 2026</strong> at Gorakhpur, Uttar Pradesh, by and between:</p>
    
    <table class="data-table">
        <tr>
            <td style="width: 25%; font-weight: bold; background-color: #f5f5f5;">FIRST PARTY<br>(Developer / Company)</td>
            <td style="width: 75%;">
                <strong>APS DREAM HOMES PVT. LTD.</strong> (CIN: U70109UP2022PTC163047), having its Registered Office at 1st Floor, APS Building, Near Ganpati Lawn, Singhariya Chauraha, Kunraghat, Gorakhpur, UP - 273008, represented through its Authorized Signatory (hereinafter referred to as the <strong>"Company / First Party"</strong>).
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="font-weight: bold; background-color: #f5f5f5;">SECOND PARTY<br>(Customer / Allottee)</td>
            <td>
                <strong>Mr./Mrs./Ms. ____________________________________________________________________</strong><br>
                Son / Wife / Daughter of: _______________________________________________________________<br>
                Permanent Address: ____________________________________________________________________<br>
                Mobile No: ________________________________ | Aadhaar / PAN No: ________________________<br>
                (hereinafter referred to as the <strong>"Allottee / Second Party"</strong>).
            </td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <div class="section-title">1. Plot &amp; Booking Particulars:</div>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Project / Township Name:</strong> __________________________________________________</li>
        <li><strong>Plot Number &amp; Block:</strong> Plot No.: ______________ | Block: ______________ | Area: ______________ Sq. Ft.</li>
        <li><strong>Total Agreed Plot Value:</strong> ₹ ________________/- (Rupees ________________________________________________________)</li>
        <li><strong>Duration Elapsed Since Booking:</strong> Approx. ________ Years / Months (Elapsed Time)</li>
        <li><strong>Booking / Token Receipt No.:</strong> __________________ | <strong>Booking Date:</strong> ____/____/20____</li>
        <li><strong>Total Token Amount Deposited:</strong> <strong>₹ ________________/-</strong> (Rupees ________________________________________________________)</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="section-title">2. Cancellation, Policy Terms &amp; Surrender of Original Documents:</div>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>Voluntary Cancellation:</strong> The Second Party (Allottee) had booked the aforesaid plot by paying an initial booking/token advance of <strong>₹ ________________/- (Rupees ________________________________________________________)</strong>. Due to personal, financial constraints, and considerable lapse of time, the Allottee is unable to proceed with the transaction and has formally and voluntarily requested the complete cancellation and termination of the booking.</li>
        <li><strong>Mandatory Physical Surrender of Originals:</strong> The Allottee hereby physically delivers, hands over, and irrevocably surrenders to the Company all <strong>Original Payment Receipts</strong>, Money Vouchers, the original <strong>Booking Application Form</strong>, Allotment Letters, and any provisional papers issued by the Company. The Allottee expressly confirms that no photocopies, digital images, or duplicates have been retained, and all rights or liens over the subject plot stand permanently surrendered and extinguished.</li>
        <li><strong>Non-Refundable Policy &amp; Complete Waiver of Heavy Default Penalties/Interest:</strong> Both parties explicitly acknowledge that as per the Company's statutory terms and official Refund Policy (Tripartite Master Deed Sections 2.1 &amp; 2.9), booking token amounts are strictly non-refundable. Furthermore, the Allottee acknowledges that following the initial token deposit, no regular monthly installments, EMI balances, or scheduled dues were cleared. Under standard contract terms, accumulated 18% penal interest, delay fees, and administrative default charges on the total plot value (₹ ________________/-) would have accumulated to a massive financial liability. However, for complete accounting clarity and on compassionate humanitarian grounds, <strong>all such accumulated interest, penalties, and defaulted liabilities are officially recorded but completely waived off and forgiven by the Company.</strong></li>
    </ol>

    <div class="section-title">3. Special Settlement, Ex-Gratia Refund &amp; Processing Timeline:</div>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>Special Ex-Gratia Consideration:</strong> Upon the special written appeal, economic hardship, and compassionate consideration of the Allottee, the Company has exceptionally agreed to release an ex-gratia partial settlement sum of:<br>
        <strong>₹ ________________/- (Rupees ________________________________________________________)</strong><br>
        as full, final, and absolute settlement, notwithstanding the non-refundable token clause and heavy interest waiver.</li>
        <li><strong>Strict Cash-Flow &amp; Processing Timeline (No Pressure Clause):</strong> The Allottee expressly understands, agrees, and acknowledges that corporate financial accounting, internal audit, and banking clearance cycles require procedural time. Therefore, the agreed settlement amount shall not be demanded immediately. The disbursement shall be processed through official corporate channels and cleared in staggered installments over a <strong>staggered liquidation cycle of up to 180 working days</strong> based on company cash-flow velocity. The Allottee explicitly covenants not to issue any legal notice, raise disputes, or exert undue coercion during this processing period.</li>
        <li><strong>Mode of Payment Realization:</strong> The settlement amount (upon maturity of processing timeline) shall be disbursed via:<br>
        [ ] Account Payee Cheque &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; [ ] Online Bank Transfer (NEFT/RTGS/IMPS/UPI) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; [ ] Cash<br>
        Cheque / UTR / Transaction No.: ____________________________________ Dated: ____/____/2026<br>
        Drawn on Bank &amp; Branch: ____________________________________________________________________</li>
        <li><strong>Waiver of Appreciation &amp; Additional Claims:</strong> The Allottee completely waives and relinquishes all claims toward market price appreciation, penal interest, compensation, or allotment rights over the aforesaid plot.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="section-title">4. Full &amp; Final Release (Irrevocable Discharge):</div>
    <p>Upon receipt of the aforesaid partial settlement amount through the due corporate process mentioned, the Allottee declares that all financial accounts, claims, rights, and disputes regarding this plot booking stand permanently and irrevocably closed. The Allottee or their legal heirs, successors, and assigns shall have no further claims, demands, suits, or rights whatsoever against the Company, its Directors, Promoters, or its projects before any Civil Court, RERA Authority, Consumer Forum, or Arbitration Tribunal in future. This Deed shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent Courts at <strong>Gorakhpur, Uttar Pradesh</strong>.</p>

    <p style="margin-top: 15px;"><strong>IN WITNESS WHEREOF,</strong> the parties hereto have signed this Cancellation and Settlement Deed on the day, month, and year first written above, having understood all terms fully in their sound state of mind.</p>

